    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster as our most potent offensive threat. With an elite score of 81.00, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Cavalli and a high-leverage leadoff spot, making him a must-start anchor. Alongside him, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) presents excellent value, leveraging a strong platoon advantage against Bassitt that elevates his utility status. We also see high upside in **Heliot Ramos** (65.50) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.68); while **Heliot Ramos** relies on assumed lineup placement, his park factor and platoon matchup against Severino provide a high ceiling, and **Sam Antonacci** continues to be a high-efficiency play given his elite xwOBA and favorable leadoff context against Taillon.\n\nOur toughest bench decision involved **Nolan Schanuel**, who finished just outside the active cut at 45.00. While his 30% recency bump is promising, the unfavorable SP skill profile of Wrobleski and the resulting risk of a suppressed offensive environment ultimately pushed the optimizer toward higher-scoring options like **Miguel Vargas** and **Liam Hicks**. Elsewhere, **Josh Lowe** remains on the bench due to a difficult platoon disadvantage against Wrobleski that significantly lowers his projected efficiency. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**; both are currently projected for the lineup, but their scoring remains sensitive to potential batting order shifts. Owners should keep a close eye on weather and final lineup confirmations, particularly as **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, further tightening our depth in the outfield as we continue to prioritize high-sprint-speed contributors to maintain our competitive edge in the SB category.",
